  "judge_reasoning": "# Evaluation Analysis\n\n## Task Requirements\nThe task asked to determine how many different types of keyboards are available when customizing a 14-inch MacBook Pro on Apple's website.\n\n## Screenshot Evidence\nReviewing the provided screenshots:\n\n1. **Screenshot 1**: Shows the \"Shop MacBook Pro\" page with the Model selection, where the **14-inch** option is selected (highlighted in blue), confirming navigation to the correct product configuration.\n\n2. **Screenshot 2**: Shows the Chip selection step of the configuration process, confirming the user is on the MacBook Pro customize page.\n\n3. **Screenshot 3**: Shows the Keyboard section in the configuration summary, which explicitly states:\n   - **Keyboard**\n   - Current: **U.S. English**\n   - **\"Choose from 20 languages\"**\n\n4. **Screenshot 4**: Shows the Keyboard section expanded with the \"Select your language\" dropdown open, displaying the language selection interface (U.S. English currently selected).\n\n## Response Verification\nThe response states there are **20 different keyboard types** and lists them: U.S. English, Arabic, British English, Chinese (Pinyin), Chinese (Zhuyin), Danish, Dutch, French Canadian, French, German, Hebrew, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, Russian, Spanish (Latin America), Spanish, Swiss, and Ukrainian — which correctly counts to 20 items.\n\nThis aligns with the screenshot evidence showing \"Choose from 20 languages\" in the Keyboard card on the 14-inch MacBook Pro configuration page.\n\n## Conclusion\nThe user successfully navigated to the 14-inch MacBook Pro customization page, located the Keyboard section, and correctly identified that 20 keyboard types (language options) are available. The answer is directly supported by the visible text \"Choose from 20 languages\" in the screenshots.\n\n**Verdict: SUCCESS**",
